# Analysis and research tooling is NOT committed. It is scratch: scripts written against one
# session's question, their scratch databases, and the notes around them. Untracked wholesale on
# 2026-09-04 (44 files) after an agent added 47 more. The files stay on disk; nothing here is
# deleted, it just does not belong in the repo.
#
# Consequence to respect: nothing tracked may DEPEND on a path under tools/. A test fixture that
# a build needs lives under mudsharp.Tests/Fixtures/Data/ instead — see npc_group_fixture.txt,
# which was moved there for exactly this reason.
tools/

# Captured wire data from the operator's own play sessions. Recordings and clogs are his game data
# and are not committed, however useful they are as test input.
#
# A test that needs real bytes does NOT get to be optional. Making one skip when its capture is
# absent was tried once (WyvernPoisonDeathReplayTests) and is a bad precedent: a protocol test that
# passes silently on a fresh clone is worse than no test, because it looks like coverage. The rule
# instead is to commit a REDACTED cut - only the frames under test, no tx records of what the owner
# typed, no stat/inventory/who rows, nothing identifying - and to negate it here by name.
*.jsonl
mudsharp.Tests/Fixtures/Data/*.jsonl
!mudsharp.Tests/Fixtures/Data/wyvern-poison-death.jsonl

# Files whose names begin with "--": always a mistyped command-line flag that a tool then treated
# as an output path. One such (`tools/combat/--db`, 217 KB of SQLite from a misplaced `--db`) was
# committed and had to be purged from history. The pattern is never a real filename here.
tools/**/--*
--*

# Allow displacement of the mucka.exe for testing, don't commit it.
mucka.exe
